g With Errors","u":"hall-of-foundations/learning-with-errors.html","k":"exhibit","h":"Foundations","c":"§157","b":"—","s":"Solve for a secret vector, then switch the noise on and watch the same algebra fail — the Learning With Errors problem beneath ML-KEM and ML-DSA.","g":["foundations","mathematics"]},{"t":"Modular Arithmetic","u":"hall-of-foundations/modular-arithmetic.html","k":"exhibit","h":"Foundations","c":"§143","b":"—","s":"Clock arithmetic, primitive roots, and the cyclic group Diffie–Hellman lives inside.","g":["foundations","mathematics","modular arithmetic","clock","primitive root","diffie-hellman"]},{"t":"The Ground Beneath the Curve","u":"hall-of-foundations/modularity-exhibit.html","k":"exhibit","h":"Foundations","c":"—","b":"—","s":"The Ground Beneath the Curve — the modularity theorem and the number theory elliptic-curve cryptography inherits.","g":["foundations","mathematics","modularity theorem","fermat","wiles","number theory","ecc"]},{"t":"The One-Way Function","u":"hall-of-foundations/one-way-function.html","k":"exhibit","h":"Foundations","c":"§146","b":"—","s":"Multiply in a blink; factor and sweat — the one-way function, conceptual keystone of modern cryptography.","g":["foundations","mathematics","one-way function","factoring","trapdoor","hardness"]},{"t":"Bilinear Pairings · Hall of Foundations","u":"hall-of-foundations/pairings.html","k":"exhibit","h":"Foundations","c":"§156","b":"—","s":"Verify a product of hidden scalars without revealing them — the bilinear pairing under zk-SNARKs.","g":["foundations","mathematics","pairing","bilinear","zk-snark","zero-knowledge","ibe"]},{"t":"Polynomial Rings · Hall of Foundations","u":"hall-of-foundations/polynomial-rings.html","k":"exhibit","h":"Foundations","c":"§153","b":"—","s":"The polynomial ring R_q = Z_q[X]/(Xⁿ+1) — the structured lattice inside ML-KEM and ML-DSA.","g":["foundations","mathematics","polynomial ring","ntt","module-lwe","ml-kem","ml-dsa","post-quantum"]},{"t":"The Prime Number T